silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_4 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegLambdaTaxExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_4 silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentLegLambdaTax', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §6.18 plus the taxonomy-as-source-leg discipline: Hom_O_01(Mittens, TaxRow_TSN_183798) = {lambda_tax}. The arrow connects Mittens to the ITIS row for Felis catus (TSN 183798); it is a typed cocone leg, NOT an identification. The hom-set being singleton, plus the parallel singleton Hom_O_01(Mittens, DomesticCat) = {lambda_cls}, distinguishes classification from taxonomy." .
